= render 'shared/breakthrough_page', page_title: 'Turniput', current_page: 'Turniput', page_subtitle: 'Making lightshow interactivity as simple as pressing a button', document_title: 'Turniput - Baldrick Board Integration Software', meta: ['No code required', 'FPP integration', 'Lamp control'], toc: turniput_toc do
  p.lead From the very beginning, we wanted to make adding interactivity as simple as point and click.

  .prose
    section#what-is-turniput
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Overview
        | What is a Turniput

      p
        | That's why the
        = link_to ' Baldrick8', board_path('baldrick8')
        |  shipped with three inputs that could control not only other Baldrick boards, but also software like FPP.
      p We've seen people connect them to beam breaks and motion sensors, but by far the most popular use has been with buttons. Pretty quickly, the requests rolled in for a way to control the button lamp too — for example, turning it off when the button couldn't be pressed.
      p
        | That led us to create the
        = link_to ' BaldrickInput1', board_path('baldrickinput1')
        | , a standalone controller dedicated to interactivity, with lamp control built in and improved
        = link_to ' Turnip Network', breakthroughs_turnip_network_path
        |  integration.
      p
        | And from there, an Input fully powered by the
        = link_to ' Turnip Network', breakthroughs_turnip_network_path
        |  was born: the
        strong  Turniput
        | .
      p Now standard across all new boards the Turniput allows easy interaction without any scripting or code.

    section#input-types
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Inputs
        | What can I use with a Turniput?

      p The Turniput is designed not only to be used with buttons but anything that can complete a circuit.

      .spec-grid
        .spec
          span.ic
            svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9"
              path d="M4 12h16M6 8l-4 4 4 4M18 8l4 4-4 4"
          h4 Beam break
          p Infrared beam interruption detection.
        .spec
          span.ic
            svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9"
              path d="M12 2v4M5 7l3 3M19 7l-3 3"
          h4 Reed switch
          p Magnetic field detection.
        .spec
          span.ic
            svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9"
              circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"
              path d="M12 2v2M12 20v2M2 12h2M20 12h2"
          h4 Motion sensor
          p Movement detection.
        .spec
          span.ic
            svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9"
              path d="M2 12h6l2-4 4 8 2-4h6"
          h4 Distance sensor
          p Proximity detection.
        .spec
          span.ic
            svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9"
              path d="M11 5L6 9H2v6h4l5 4V5zM15 9l4 4M19 9l-4 4"
          h4 Sound sensor
          p Audio level detection.
        .spec
          span.ic
            svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9"
              circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"
              path d="M12 8v8M8 12h8"
          h4 Buttons
          p Physical button controls — still the most popular.

    section#lamp-control
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Lamps
        | Turniput lamp control

      p If you are using the Turniput with a button that has an LED in it, our lamp controls allow you to set the status of the LED depending on the Turniput status — On, Off or Breathe.

      .lamp-grid
        .lamp
          .lamp-dot.on
          h4 On
          p LED stays lit.
        .lamp
          .lamp-dot.off
          h4 Off
          p LED stays off.
        .lamp
          .lamp-dot.breathe
          h4 Breathe
          p LED pulses slowly.

    section#fpp-integration
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot FPP
        | FPP integration

      p The Turnip Network automatically detects FPP instances on your network and using the API will seamlessly pull in playlists and sequences allowing you to start a show, manage the volume and/or play a specific (or random) song at the touch of a button.
      p If you like to get your hands dirty with the FPP commands, Turniputs give you full access to all of them from within the Baldrick interface.

    section#webhook-integration
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Webhooks
        | Webhook integration

      p When an input is triggered you can send a GET request to a specific URL (either on your network or over the internet) — perfect for logging or any other online effects you have for your show.

    .callout.info
      span.ic
        svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
          circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"
          path d="M12 16v-4M12 8h.01"
      div
        span.lbl Pair it up
        p.bd
          | Turniputs work best alongside the
          = link_to ' Turnip Network', breakthroughs_turnip_network_path
          |  — boards discover each other and FPP installs without you writing a line of code.

    h2
      span.hk
        span.bar
        span.annot Keep reading
      | Related breakthroughs

    .next-grid
      = link_to breakthroughs_turnip_network_path, class: 'next-card' do
        .top
          span.kind Breakthrough
          span.go →
        h4 The Turnip Network
        p Board discoverability and FPP auto-detection across your show.
      = link_to board_path('baldrickinput1'), class: 'next-card' do
        .top
          span.kind Docs
          span.go →
        h4 BaldrickInput1
        p The dedicated interactivity controller with lamp control built in.
      = link_to breakthroughs_cunningfx_path, class: 'next-card' do
        .top
          span.kind Breakthrough
          span.go →
        h4 CunningFX
        p Trigger presets from inputs across the network.
      = link_to breakthroughs_path, class: 'next-card' do
        .top
          span.kind Index
          span.go →
        h4 All breakthroughs
        p Explore everything that makes Baldrick boards a bit special.

